From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maslow <wangfugen@126.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:46:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the threaded WAL Home alive through teardown

Cancel home tasks, destroy the resident roots and then cancel any facet drains those roots scheduled. Keep the actor index, isolate copy and WAL channel alive for observer cleanup, shipper deregistration and SQLite close callbacks. Own the spare descriptor until task cleanup ends.

Exercise scope teardown with production root and facet actors, real SQLite connections and lifetime markers that verify pending task cancellation, both CLOSED callbacks and actor index cleanup.

